#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119652 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](images/64/64a3661b0699fbde542ed1709bacf569f681477a5f824f0650b07d9060b82dae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} {:answer/id #uuid "96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442968} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442970} {:answer/id #uuid "f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442976} {:answer/id #uuid "fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108308" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,2,1⟩+t⟨3,0,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=13.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ ⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ 1(-1+3t)-2+2(1+2t) & =13 \\\\ -1+3t-2+2+4t & =13 \\\\ 7t & =14 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+3(2),2,1+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,2,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442960} {:answer/id #uuid "0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442961} {:answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} {:answer/id #uuid "66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442965} {:answer/id #uuid "bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" :question/math-academy-id "q-108315" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-3,4⟩+t⟨4,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ ⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ -2(1+4t)+(-3)(-3-2t)+2\\cdot (4+t) & =1 \\\\ -2-8t+9+6t+8+2t & =1 \\\\ 15 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "600b8aef-da6c-5a05-9753-24914a3499d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242041} {:answer/id #uuid "7687f722-fb74-5a86-8afb-5ba790d4f143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242232} {:answer/id #uuid "a77e3a01-860e-5d47-a380-4a2919fe0ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242649} {:answer/id #uuid "b30eea27-088d-5354-8ef8-bcf626ddf460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} {:answer/id #uuid "f57050d6-b5e9-5c5f-838d-d66ca290b074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b30eea27-088d-5354-8ef8-bcf626ddf460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} :answer-field/id #uuid "6652b296-a21e-518a-9c5b-d45f374f2267" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d4770f9-017d-5451-ade2-ef9bc61cba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-108323" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0979ee26-b4dd-5ed5-9cab-237f13bab300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241262} {:answer/id #uuid "50818f44-1865-5083-bcf9-14855607c5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241899} {:answer/id #uuid "8aff1c43-eaae-5c07-92ca-05a88e6a5417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242409} {:answer/id #uuid "b9391f01-11c7-5c3a-9ff7-274ffb356b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242804} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c8e226-835f-5977-879f-0773d4b64c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6c8e226-835f-5977-879f-0773d4b64c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e65bb2ef-90c6-598e-9157-9a8edd5838b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23026cc4-61f1-51ff-9518-0d934ee1dfc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-108325" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476e5895-586f-57b1-a8e9-64b9c347e830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241826} {:answer/id #uuid "65e0041a-b33d-5596-9117-8e8c8d122a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242098} {:answer/id #uuid "b19a65f8-95fd-5d04-a4c0-b580feed54f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,13,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242728} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bc4d15-10e0-5455-a652-8f5fec3c26f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,-1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242748} {:answer/id #uuid "e16af936-42d1-5d0e-b45e-142ec3fb9818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e16af936-42d1-5d0e-b45e-142ec3fb9818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243183} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd38d870-1520-58ab-a4ad-250e4f90b837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba20f45e-ea9a-5cbd-a036-8965c362108b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbd933f-3f29-5070-8231-31ef77e6f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(20,29,40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399631} {:answer/id #uuid "f073d53a-a8e7-5ae2-82c8-e5cb31403d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-23,-25)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399632} {:answer/id #uuid "654434c9-d7c4-5e1e-bfe8-aaafc9425c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-7,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399633} {:answer/id #uuid "509a688f-9e49-51a5-95ba-17bf03e47002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399634} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec3fa5-fe3a-5ef1-bb6e-18d2712b8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,9,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec3fa5-fe3a-5ef1-bb6e-18d2712b8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,9,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399635} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4bd1c19-a96b-51b8-b83f-2c4bebba5b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ee9813a-b1b3-5ef0-86f7-ac30b2000775" :question/math-academy-id "q-108368" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "613bfe5f-02e2-5735-9f79-164b162ce348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442964} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b4a532-3b78-5ed1-a6e7-746b7ec7ab3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-3,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442969} {:answer/id #uuid "d748dd3f-d487-5117-bef8-07f995fa3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442974} {:answer/id #uuid "de970a68-1f18-57df-a82c-3fb7858ebc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442975} {:answer/id #uuid "f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442977} :answer-field/id #uuid "817f92e5-c306-5bc0-98bb-5216ce23f4dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-108369" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,1,4⟩+t⟨3,2,-6⟩,\\,Π:-4x+3y-z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3y-z-11 & =0 \\\\ -4x+3y-z & =11 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ -4(-2+3t)+3(1+2t)-(4-6t) & =11 \\\\ 8-12t+3+6t-4+6t & =11 \\\\ 7 & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c181d54f-7b5e-5e40-b660-5db606239a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399652} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2c2f01-60e6-5197-ae47-76dd272575a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399653} {:answer/id #uuid "100fc206-faa0-5c9a-8c1d-f828c27459ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} {:answer/id #uuid "a03ac96b-8e87-5579-959e-6059ecf3486c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399655} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d8eeca-91ef-5d44-a9a1-da7d1707ffce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "100fc206-faa0-5c9a-8c1d-f828c27459ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd4a0b3-55ce-54d3-98c8-8b7021d46e30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" :question/math-academy-id "q-108889" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9884d5e8-c0d4-5eb6-9188-a7a52f27eb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117518} {:answer/id #uuid "266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442963} {:answer/id #uuid "676389da-d8bf-5b92-bcd7-a398a98b3965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442966} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bcd1a1-4127-5759-8dbc-c749468c35cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442972} {:answer/id #uuid "cfddec79-fecc-5697-9dc1-640959c5e5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4728cad-b3da-5e14-bea1-edda7db46313" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d936aa91-f337-5522-833b-6e328b8ac933" :question/math-academy-id "q-33068" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩=4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2(3+2t)-2t+4(1+t) & =4 \\\\ 6+4t-2t+4+4t & =4 \\\\ 6t & =-6 \\\\ t & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(-1),2(-1),1+(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,-2,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153f3c4f-9bb4-575a-bf5e-88b04e29d58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302595} {:answer/id #uuid "75ca0ec4-f115-5eaf-8978-84b0e49468fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303175} {:answer/id #uuid "a800de77-92dc-5141-bd29-c54cd12e4e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} {:answer/id #uuid "cd43b129-2b04-51da-afc7-ea0b002f1f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303723} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b25123-f5a5-5705-961f-c56f3f92d28c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,19)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a800de77-92dc-5141-bd29-c54cd12e4e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba170b3-1e35-5d70-ae58-276390f33698" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9c8b702-f6a3-5488-9345-1b22f3aeec01" :question/math-academy-id "q-33081" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩=19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,1,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,0,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ccad579-7ffd-5028-82c9-8be517c44ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a96f69-83dc-57ab-88b1-de0764e272b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,2,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303669} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88a9e0-a58d-507d-8dbf-f29575569623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303833} {:answer/id #uuid "f8782171-7da4-599e-a483-393f0200a20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304012} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f6c3e0-0705-5423-bdeb-301d579540f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ccad579-7ffd-5028-82c9-8be517c44ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0993881-1ebc-59b3-9c71-cbd4dfde3c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c249fd8c-dcff-5201-89e1-bb6d2a206072" :question/math-academy-id "q-33201" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee24fdf4-e1ee-5f88-bc78-1cd69107c3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402258} {:answer/id #uuid "3cff9213-8332-5106-9a38-96d7ec4a4378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7ebdfb-49aa-56f4-a0ad-f4d48aa68b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402260} {:answer/id #uuid "6adfa3c5-c5cd-56cd-841d-1fd0fc016077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402261} {:answer/id #uuid "cd22fb61-25ce-5f17-bad1-fbd4ce2f0694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd22fb61-25ce-5f17-bad1-fbd4ce2f0694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e05243-350c-5a1d-ad1e-5c71c37318cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb8f532-8109-56ef-8ea6-7d7e8fda174e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,31,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312080} {:answer/id #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f8512a-48d0-5872-a500-e1de657bfe34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,13,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313291} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b9d8a5-8b12-541b-b956-720a78e83b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313762} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cde894-634d-5f97-9e4d-09a5ae155357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-20,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} :answer-field/id #uuid "85681f3e-c4a0-5f09-ab05-6853a3e1d4ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f60e171f-8d34-5a7f-bcb5-85d2254301da" :question/math-academy-id "q-33988" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+t⟨-5,2,7⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩=30.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ ⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20,13,31⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a8eacf-acaa-535b-84fd-68dd0e55e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339449} {:answer/id #uuid "9245627b-7ed9-5a81-a591-0bddaf5c1488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340440} {:answer/id #uuid "95647350-28b0-50f0-ba88-074ca618981c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340476} {:answer/id #uuid "a8076978-e0f4-543d-834d-5fa159290d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} {:answer/id #uuid "cce78ef0-b9c9-5c65-96ff-bcf9b11be57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8076978-e0f4-543d-834d-5fa159290d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} :answer-field/id #uuid "75a90e21-4110-5920-b29a-9528326a3c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a27e98ee-3a96-559d-b75b-2bf4d0ce11d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5220f57b-422e-531b-842b-1f584644f261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339883} {:answer/id #uuid "979f8148-7b8d-5ec3-a55e-fb37aea141d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340493} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d885e-e879-51ab-96e4-b43985498ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340786} {:answer/id #uuid "bb602b66-8066-5891-8e86-1da45546964a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} {:answer/id #uuid "bba3c359-7475-5f71-8622-34809c6c9b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb602b66-8066-5891-8e86-1da45546964a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} :answer-field/id #uuid "10fba32d-90d3-5858-a355-57f3ffefce29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d4d8f0f-1eab-5bd0-8f71-a26637e6257d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"}]}
